# --- secrets: never commit ---
# geminiAPI.txt is NOT the only copy of the key. `.geminiAPI` (dotfile, same
# 53-char value) and `.zshrc` (holds a live ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN) were both
# caught STAGED on 2026-08-25, before the first commit. Re-check with
#   git diff --cached --name-only | grep -iE "gemini|zshrc|rc$|env|key|token"
# before EVERY commit, not just the first one.
geminiAPI.txt
.geminiAPI
.geminiAPI*
*gemini*key*
# ...but a .py file under current/ is CODE, not a credential. `*gemini*key*` was
# silently ignoring current/gemini_key.py, so it stayed untracked and a fresh
# checkout LOST it -- proven by its absence from a new worktree, which made
# nonrouted_baseline.py (RQ2) unimportable.
#
# That was first patched as `!current/gemini_key.py`, one filename. On 2026-08-25
# the SAME bug immediately recurred on current/rotate_gemini_key.py, because a
# per-filename negation does not generalise. So negate by RULE instead: every
# .py in current/ is the author's own source and belongs in git. Credentials in
# this repo are .txt / dotfiles / .env / .key / .pem -- never .py.
#
# This does NOT weaken the secret guard, because a filename pattern could never
# catch a key *embedded* in a file anyway. That is the pre-commit CONTENT scan's
# job, and it is the check that actually matters:
#   git diff --cached -U0 | grep -c "$(cat geminiAPI.txt)"     # must print 0
!current/*.py
.zshrc
.bashrc
.profile
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- virtualenv ---
# .venv*/ also covers .venv-pdf/ (pdf-skill tooling, kept out of the pinned
# thesis venv so the torch/transformers pins stay reproducible).
.venv*/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- API / model caches -------------------------------------------------
# These are large and machine-local, BUT read the caching rule before you
# decide to delete any of them: thesis numbers come from a single cached run,
# and Gemini query generation is non-deterministic without its cache. Ignoring
# them in git is fine; deleting them mid-experiment is not.
*_cache.json
verifier_cache*.json
relational_cache.json
relational_retrieval_cache.json
relational_nli_cache.json
llm_baseline_cache.json
*.json.bak-*
archive/caches/

# --- large, re-downloadable, or derived (keeps history reviewable) ---------
# data/ is FActScore + FEVER (54M, re-downloadable). factscore-repo is an
# embedded git clone -- git warns about it and it is re-clonable.
data/
factscore-repo/
*.zip
*.pdf
papers_analysis/downloaded_pdfs/

# --- OS noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- scratch ---
/tmp/
*.tmp
*.log
.agents/
.claude/
